reply.body:
I think doing a `MUST` always is OK. We will rewrite it appropriately as necessary back to a filter if it doesn't require scoring.

As for `COMPLETE` vs `COMPLETE_NO_SCORES` we should update this weight factory supplier to accept the sub-aggregators. The sub-aggregators shouldn't change throughout the life-time of the aggregator on the shard. So continuing to have the same weight once its cached is ok. 

But, I would take a look at the sub-aggregators, and their provided `scoreMode()` values. This will indicate to us if we need to provide `MUST` & `COMPLETE` vs `FILTER` & `COMPLETE_NO_SCORES`.

There are examples of this all around the code base,

```
        ScoreMode scoreMode = null;
        for (BucketCollector collector : collectors) {
            if (scoreMode == null) {
                scoreMode = collector.scoreMode();
            } else if (scoreMode != collector.scoreMode()) {
                return ScoreMode.COMPLETE;
            }
        }
        return scoreMode;
```
^ how the multi-bucket collectors work. 

But aggregators will provide `scoreMode()` and the score mode we use should be based off that if possible

